{"url": "http://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/future_students/graduates.php", "final_url": "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/graduates/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Graduates - Electrical and Computer Engineering\nSkip to content\nMenu\nHome\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate Home\nComputer Engineering\nElectrical Engineering\nDual Degree in ECE + Biomedical Engineering\nAccelerated B.S./Master\u2019s Program\nAdvising and Resources\nCourses\nGraduate\nGraduate Home\nComputer Engineering\nElectrical Engineering\nOnline Programs\nAccelerated B.S./Master\u2019s Program\nAdmissions\nCourses\nAdvising\nStudent Resources\nResearch\nFacilities\nPeople\nIndustry & Alumni\nIndustrial Advisory Board\nEngineer in Residence\nCSU Alumni Association\nGive\nGive Now\nAbout\nSearch for:\nElectrical and Computer Engineering Walter Scott, Jr. College of Engineering\nGraduate programs\nAdvance\nyour education\nand your career\nDegree Programs\nComputer Engineering\nElectrical Engineering\nOnline Programs\nAccelerated B.S./Master\u2019s Program\nAdmissions\nCourses\nAdvising\nStudent Resources\nDegree Programs\nComputer Engineering\nElectrical Engineering\nOnline Programs\nAccelerated B.S./Master\u2019s Program\nAdmissions\nCourses\nAdvising\nStudent Resources\nHow will you\nEngineer a World of Difference?\nShape your future with flexible, customizable programs built for your goals. Our world-leading professors will equip you with deep expertise, broad perspective, and the mindset to lead in a rapidly evolving world.\nExplore on-campus programs\nExplore online programs\nRequest appointment to learn more\nStart your application now\nMaster's Programs in Computer Engineering\nBe the intelligence behind artificial and intelligence and future computing technologies.\nMaster's Programs in Electrical Engineering\nDrive technologies that guide everything from self-driving cars to healthcare devices.\nPh.D. Programs in Computer Engineering\nAdvance your career and become a subject-matter expert in your area of interest.\nPh.D. Programs in Electrical Engineering\nEngage in research that excites you and pushes the boundaries of technology.\nExplore\nOnline Programs\nOnline certificates\nAerospace Satellites, Radars, and Remote Sensing\nComputer Systems Engineering\nData Engineering\nEmbedded Systems\nOnline Degree Programs in Electrical Engineering\nOnline learning with real-world impact.\nOnline Degree Programs in Computer Engineering\nSame CSU faculty. Same CSU standards.\nGet Started Now (ECE Online Programs)\nGet Started Now (On-campus Programs)\nGain skills for a diverse range of industries.\nMachine Learning + AI \u2022 Space + Aerospace \u2022 Computer Chip Design \u2022 Embedded + IoT Systems \u2022 Computer Networks, Information Systems, and Cybersecurity \u2022 Biosciences, Biomedical Engineering, and Health Sciences \u2022 Power + Energy Systems \u2022 Manufacturing \u2022 Healthcare Systems\n$110,000\nAverage base salary, M.S. electrical engineering\n$114,000\nAverage base salary, M.S. computer engineering\n$132,000\nAverage base salary, Ph.D. Electrical & Computer Engineering\nAdmission and Program Details\nLearn more about our requirements, objectives, and program details.\nApply Now\nStart your graduate application today!\nAdvising and Student Resources\nSchedule an appointment with our graduate advisor and plan your academic journey.\nWhy Electrical & Computer Engineering at CSU?\nStudy with experts, build your knowledge, and stand out in your field.\nEngage in research in a top 10 technology producing department at CSU.\nGain skills and credentials to advance innovation in virtually any field.\nTailor your learning experience through customizable and flexible curriculum.\nLearn from professors who are recognized worldwide for their excellence.\nGain access to career and internship opportunities in our thriving tech corridor.\n'Journey to a prosperous career'\nCSU\u2019s Electrical and Computer Engineering program is more than a curriculum - it's a journey to a prosperous career, embraced by a community that fosters growth. One standout feature of the program is its flexibility. This distinctive opportunity enhances our overall learning experience and aligns perfectly with the ever-evolving field of computer engineering.\"\nDivyani Thota, CSU Computer Engineering Alum\nOutstanding Online Learner\nDistance learner balanced courses with her full-time job at HP Inc.\nEngineering Policy Fellow\nMaster's student discusses policy-making for sustainable computing\nPh.D. Student Spotlight\nAI researcher selected for NASA early-career research team\n10 Cool Things: AI and ECE\nNotable examples of how the ECE department is shaping the future of AI.\nRead more news\nReturn to Top\nCSU Engineering Building, B104\n1373 Campus Delivery\nFort Collins, CO 80523-1373\n(970) 491-6600\nResources\nDepartment Code\nContact us\nEngineering Human Resources\nEngineering Business Office (EBO)\nEngineering Success Center\nCollege News\nCollege Home Page\nDepartment of Atmospheric Science\nDepartment of Civil & Environmental Engineering\nDepartment of Electrical & Computer Engineering\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering\nDepartment of Systems Engineering\nSchool of Materials Science and Engineering\nSchool of Biomedical & Chemical Engineering\nCooperative Institute for Research in the Atmosphere (CIRA)\nApply to CSU\nAccessibility Statement\nDisclaimer\nEqual Opportunity\nPrivacy Statement\n\u00a9 2026 Colorado State University, Fort Collins, Colorado 80523 USA\nGive Now", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/graduates/#page"], ["Home", "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/undergraduates/"], ["Undergraduate Home", "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/undergraduates/"], ["Computer Engineering", "https://www.engr.colostate.edu/ece/undergraduates/computer-engineering-undergrad/"], ["Electrical Engineering", "ht